==Strategy==
Due to [[Heavenly Herald Papuu|Papuu]]'s immense Omni Strike range and guaranteed to chance to deal 40% [[Toxic]] damage, you should expect to replace non-[[:Category:Cats with Toxic Immunity|Toxic-immune]] small units frequently. It's very difficult to prevent Papuu from ever damaging the [[Cat Base]], but not impossible with hypermaxed units and a perfect run. Luckily, Toxic doesn't affect the Cat Base, hence having more Cat Base health (from levels, [[Ototo Corps|Ototo Corps]] and [[Cat Combo]]s) buys you more time to continue fighting.

It is also recommended that you try to defeat two (or all three) Dagshunds before moving onto Papuu. If you trigger her Strengthen ability before killing two or three of the Dagshunds, she can destroy your base much faster when dealing with the last Dagshund (though this probably doesn't matter if your cats are at a high enough level).

Much like Daboo, Papuu is immune to knockback effects (including the [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast]] [[Cat Cannon|Cannon]]). She is additionally Wave Immune, meaning [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]] is the only battle item able to keep her away from your base. Since she isn't immune to curse, the [[Ototo Corps#Curseblast|Curseblast]] can help buy some additional time, which could make all the difference in battle as long as it manages to dismiss a single Toxic attack.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Talented Riceball Cat]]: With the [[Immune to Toxic]] [[Talents|Talent]], he can really help with stalling Papuu and the peons without getting harmed by the notorious Toxic effect.
*[[Vega Cat (Rare Cat)|Vega Cat]]: Works just like Riceball, he can work as your secondary meatshield alongside Riceball. Investing into him is recommended due to his relatively low base HP.
*[[Bakery Cat (Rare Cat)|Fried Chicken Cat]]: If timed precisely, Fried Chicken can get a hit on Papuu and Curse her, removing her Toxic ability, though he will have to be frequently replaced.
*Talented [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Can greatly aid you in battle with the Extra Money and Move Speed Up Talents as it can go to the frontline quickly, do some damage, and give you a lot of cash if used right.
*[[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]]: With Food Stall Cat's [[True Form]], the stage becomes much easier as Cafeteria Cat's Curse, combined with its Massive Damage to [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]] and fast speed allows it to both remove Papuu's Toxic and quickly whittle her down, being more consistent than Fried Chicken at that regard.
*[[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Teacher BearCat]]: Although his slow speed may be a hinderance, proper timing allows him to quickly handle the Wall Doges, as well as occasionally damage the Dagshund. Be careful not to send too many, or else he may drain your wallet.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]]: Given its speed, Extra Money ability, and high damage, it can be used to damage the Sir Rels before they push too far and grant you additional cash in the process.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasa Jizo]]: Kasa Jizo is a highly disposable anti-Angel midranger with Massive Damage to them. Easily replaceable when lost, damage from individual Jizos can accumulate quickly.
*[[Lasvoss (Uber Rare Cat)|Lasvoss Reborn]]: Lasvoss gains Toxic immunity in True Form and is a great choice for dealing heavy direct damage as a midranger.
*[[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]]: A Talented Greater Balrog is essentially a stronger Can Can, able to melt strong peons and deal heavy damage to Papuu.
*[[Hades the Punisher (Uber Rare Cat)|Hades the Deathdealer]]: His immunity to Toxic and tremendous health allow him to tank many Papuu hits. With the right support, Hades can keep her away long enough for you to win the fight.
*[[Kintaro (Uber Rare Cat)|Kinrangers Gigaforce]]: In True Form, Kinrangers have a high chance to curse Angel enemies, rendering Papuu a non-threat. Just time Kinrangers whenever the path to Papuu is clear and fire the Curseblast Cannon to prevent her Toxic ability from damaging them.
*[[Kalisa (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kalisa]]: Not very effective when Papuu isn't cursed, but can deliver crushing blows to her nonetheless. Just make sure you have enough money and there are no peons in the way. Speed Up Talents will improve her time getting to Papuu and, therefore, her time in the battle.
*[[Shitakiri Sparrow (Uber Rare Cat)|Chunchun Haunters]]: Similar in usage of Kinrangers Gigaforce, they can also curse Papuu and disable her Toxic attacks. You also need to time them whenever the path to Papuu is clear.
*[[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli, Daughter of Chaos]]: Much like Kinrangers Gigaforce and Chunchun Haunters, the [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] variant of [[Kasli the Scourge (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli]] can curse Papuu to disable her Toxic ability and also deal with other threats, making it that much easier for support to tag along. Papuu is not Immune to Surge, so Kasli can also contribute significant damage against both her and the nasty peons.
*[[Iz the Dancer of Grief (Uber Rare Cat)|Iz the Lady of Mourning]]: Her manageable cost, Toxic Immunity, Curse Immunity and massive damage to [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless Enemies]] make her invaluable here. Even at Level 30, she makes this stage a joke once summoned.
*[[One-Eyed Asuka (Uber Rare Cat)|Blue-Eyed Asuka]]: She has Immune to Toxic, and is able to Curse Papuu just like her original counterpart. However, it should be noted that she has a fairly poor uptime on her Curse.

